course: dictionary
lesson: 10300
title: Toughen: stronger and stricter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To toughen something means to make it stronger and harder to break or damage. «Guitar strings hurt beginners' fingertips; after a few weeks of short regular practice, the skin toughens into calluses.» The skin does not get weaker. It becomes harder, so it can take more.
explain: You can also toughen a person, or toughen up. To toughen up means to become stronger and better at dealing with difficult things. Some people say it unkindly, to tell someone to stop complaining. Read the whole sentence to see which kind of toughen it is.
explain: In the news, toughen can mean to make rules or laws stricter. «The government toughened the rules.» Nothing physical has changed here. Ask yourself: is something being made harder, or is it being made stricter?
fact: Toughen is a verb: toughen, toughens, toughened, toughening.
fact: «Toughen» means to make something stronger and harder to break or damage.
fact: «Toughened glass» is heated and cooled so it is stronger, and it breaks into small, blunt pieces.
fact: «Toughen up» means to become stronger and better at dealing with difficult things.
fact: «Toughen» can also mean to make rules or laws stricter.
exercise: «Guitar strings hurt beginners' fingertips; after a few weeks, the skin toughens into calluses.» What happens to the skin? | It turns into a string | It becomes thinner and softer | It stops feeling anything at all | *It becomes harder and stronger
exercise: «Car side windows are toughened glass that breaks into small blunt pieces.» What is the good thing about toughened glass? | *It breaks into small, blunt pieces | It is made of soft wood | It never breaks, even when hit hard | It is exactly the same as ordinary glass
exercise: «The government toughened the rules.» What does toughened mean here? | Thrown away | Made shorter | *Made stricter | Made softer and more relaxed
test: «Phone screens are toughened glass, treated so the surface is harder; a drop on a corner can still crack them.» Why can a phone screen still crack? | Phone screens are made of paper | Toughened glass cannot be made harder than it is | *A hard drop on a corner can still crack it | Phone screens are never dropped
test: Mia says, «Toughen up, it's only a scratch!» What does she mean? | Be quieter and softer about it | Put a hard cover on the scratch | *Be braver and stop complaining about it | Make the scratch bigger
exam: «Sam had to toughen up after the cold, wet training week.» What does toughen up mean here? | Forgot his kit at home | *Became stronger and better at coping with hard things | Became wetter and colder | Became quieter and shyer
